Subject: [PATCH] determine the output object without depending on rev

build_wrapper.sh extracted the -o argument by shelling out to `rev`, which is
part of util-linux and is not present in every build image (notably the
conda-forge alma10 image). When `rev` is missing the extraction silently
yields garbage, nm is then invoked with no operand, the symbol list comes out
empty and objcopy is never run. The fat runtime components are left with
unprefixed symbols and the final link fails with undefined references to
avx2_*, corei7_*, simde_* and friends.

Walk the argument list instead, which needs no external tools and is not
confused by paths containing spaces, and fail loudly rather than silently
producing an unrenamed object.

diff --git a/cmake/build_wrapper.sh b/cmake/build_wrapper.sh
index 32bdf1c..cf8d143 100755
--- a/cmake/build_wrapper.sh
+++ b/cmake/build_wrapper.sh
@@ -12,7 +12,19 @@ PREFIX=$1
 KEEPSYMS_IN=$2
 shift 2
 # $@ contains the actual build command
-OUT=$(echo "$@" | rev | cut -d ' ' -f 2- | rev | sed 's/.* -o \(.*\.o\).*/\1/')
+# The output object is the argument following the last -o.
+OUT=
+_prev=
+for _arg in "$@"; do
+    if [ "${_prev}" = "-o" ]; then
+        OUT=${_arg}
+    fi
+    _prev=${_arg}
+done
+if [ -z "${OUT}" ]; then
+    echo "$0: could not determine the output object from the build command" >&2
+    exit 1
+fi
 trap cleanup INT QUIT EXIT
 SYMSFILE=$(mktemp -p /tmp ${PREFIX}_rename.syms.XXXXX)
 KEEPSYMS=$(mktemp -p /tmp keep.syms.XXXXX)
